Reason:  
All three scripts return the same numerical output, but `1result.sql` achieves the task with the shortest, clearest logic:

• A single CTE (`city_totals`) already filters to the five cities with the lowest summed payments, so no extra nesting is needed.  
• It correctly sums the full payment per city and counts delivered orders with `COUNT(DISTINCT o.order_id)`, eliminating any risk of over‑counting when an order has multiple payment rows.  
• The final `SELECT` immediately computes the two required averages, giving the correct answer in the most concise way.